From 26465923103080c986e536011d8a3d5ff71173f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:24:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(agc): reuse a data-only draw stage rebased to moved
 user-data pointers (APS5_REBASED_STAGE_REUSE)

A data-only draw candidate required every used user word to be bit-identical,
so stages whose per-frame ring pointers moved were captured and materialized
again. With the switch on, a candidate whose differing used words are pure
base pointers (asBase and not asValue, with runs read through them) is copied
with those runs shifted by the pointer delta and its forwarded shader-data
words patched, then validated against the memory at the new addresses; data
words at known positions are refreshed with patchDataWords. Any other change
(value words, vertex fetch words, image tables, BDA writes, differing
contents) falls back to the full path. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
